```rust
/// The one clause the first-scored ledger's own integrity adds to either note,
/// or `None` for the ordinary clean ledger.
///
/// Shared by [`unhittable_note`] (the live seam) and [`retrospective_note`]
/// (the pass), so the two cannot drift into two spellings of one fact - the
/// "two doors, one policy, one deaf" shape this repo has shipped seven times.
///
/// Why it has to be said at all: a line that fails to parse means
/// [`read_first_scored`] has no record for whatever path it named, so
/// `first_scored_age` returns `None` and the surprise lands in `unmeasurable`
/// - byte-identical to a path the scorer has never seen. The count is the only
/// thing that separates "this ledger is corrupt" from "this project has not
/// scored that file yet", and it was already computed and thrown away
/// (Day 210; the same silence #764 fixed one ledger over).
pub(crate) fn dropped_ledger_clause(dropped: usize) -> Option<String> {
    (dropped > 0).then(|| {
        let noun = if dropped == 1 { "line" } else { "lines" };
        format!(
            "; {dropped} malformed {noun} in the first-scored ledger - \
             those paths read as unmeasured, not as having no record"
        )
    })
}
```

